From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:52:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Send a Disassociation frame on the link of its BSS

hostapd_drv_sta_disassoc() passes a link ID only for a non-AP MLD. For
any other station of an AP MLD, i802_sta_disassoc() sends the frame with
link ID -1, so nl80211 uses the frequency of the first link of the
interface, while the SA and the BSSID are the link address of the BSS.
If that BSS is not the first link, ieee80211_mgmt_tx() in mac80211 finds
the frame off the channel of its link and refuses it with -EBUSY. The
station does not get the Disassociation frame.

Pass the link ID of the BSS for every station of an AP MLD, as
hostapd_drv_sta_deauth() does.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -931,10 +931,9 @@ int hostapd_drv_sta_disassoc(struct host
 	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
 		struct sta_info *sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, addr);
 
-		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta)) {
+		link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta))
 			own_addr = hapd->mld->mld_addr;
-			link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
-		}
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
